{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MolecularConstruction.AufbauOpenStrandPerron","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MolecularConstruction.AufbauOpenStrandPerron","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.closed_key_exceeds_open","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.closed_key_exceeds_open","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/aufbau-open-strand-perron.lean#L87-L97","doc":"**Closed key exceeds the open (Madelung) key by one extra `q^ℓ`.** The\nopen-strand total weight `q^{n+ℓ}` (Madelung key `n+ℓ`) and the\nrotation-invariant closed total `q^{n+2ℓ}` (key `n+2ℓ`, the predicted ordering)\ndiffer by exactly the extra angular factor `q^ℓ`: `q^{n+2ℓ} = q^{n+ℓ} · q^ℓ`. The\nempirical Madelung order is the open key; the canonical (rotation-invariant)\nobservable predicts the closed key. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.closed_loop_is_open_squared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.closed_loop_is_open_squared","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/aufbau-open-strand-perron.lean#L77-L85","doc":"**Rotation-invariant (closed-loop) reading is the SQUARE of the open one.**\nThe `a=+2` weight `q^{2ℓ}` — the q-dimension / top weight `q^{2ℓ}` of the\npackaged `(2ℓ+1)`-dim irrep `V_ℓ`, the rotation-invariant trace that *is* the\nisolated atom's energy — equals the **square** of the open-strand weight `q^ℓ`.\nSo the Aufbau `a=+1` vs `a=+2` gap is `open` vs `open²`: the isolated-atom\nsymmetry (a trace) selects the closed reading `a=+2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.perron_eigenvalue_is_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.perron_eigenvalue_is_q","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/aufbau-open-strand-perron.lean#L61-L75","doc":"**Perron dominance — the dominant eigenvalue is `q` on every block.** For the\nsubstrate `q > 1`, the eigenvalue `q` strictly dominates `−q⁻¹` in modulus:\n`|−q⁻¹| = q⁻¹ < q = |q|`. So the dominant (largest-modulus) eigenvalue of every\nHecke generator is `q`, independent of the representation — an **open** strand\n(Perron-dominated transfer element) weighs `q^L` on *every* block. (This does\n*not* by itself give the orbital energy: the isolated atom's energy is the\nrotation-invariant trace, not the open-strand matrix element — see file\ndocstring.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.hecke_eigenvalue_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.hecke_eigenvalue_mem","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/aufbau-open-strand-perron.lean#L50-L59","doc":"**Eigenvalues on every block.** Any eigenvalue `x` of the Hecke generator —\na root of its quadratic, which holds in *every* representation — is one of the\ntwo roots `q` or `−q⁻¹`. The eigenvalue spectrum `{q, −q⁻¹}` is therefore\nrepresentation-independent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.hecke_quadratic_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.hecke_quadratic_factor","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/aufbau-open-strand-perron.lean#L41-L48","doc":"**Hecke quadratic factors.** Over `ℝ` with `q ≠ 0`, the Hecke characteristic\npolynomial `x² − (q−q⁻¹)x − 1` factors as `(x − q)(x + q⁻¹)`. This is the\ndefining quadratic of the generator `σ_i` (`σ² = (q−q⁻¹)σ + 1`), valid in every\nrepresentation. ","signatureChunk":0}]}